horts, sporting an Apple watch and Jean-Michel Basquiat-inspired T-shirt, thumbing his notes for his first address at the summit on Tuesday.", "reference": "2022 November 15, Patrick Wintour, “Sergei Lavrov, a fixture of Russian diplomacy facing his toughest test in Ukraine”, in The Guardian:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive, with through) To turn the pages of (a book) in order to read it cursorily.", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": ["thumb through", "I thumbed through the book and decided not to bother reading it all."], "quotes": [{"text": "It is also disconcerting when you suddenly realise that the driver isn't steering, but may be thumbing over his Customs papers with his feet up.", "reference": "1948 March and April, “Notes and News: Lines in County Donegal”, in Railway Magazine, page 129:"}], "synonyms": ["peruse", "flip through"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "прелиствам"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "翻閱 /翻阅"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "selailla"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "feuilleter"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "durchblättern"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "листа́ть"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "проли́стывать"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "перели́стывать"}, {"language": {"code": "tr", "name": "Turkish"}, "word": "sayfaları karıştırmak"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To gesture with the thumb, for example when flagging a ride.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Oh, look! There’s a car coming! Thumb-no, wave. They probably don’t understand thumbing.", "reference": "1977, Diana Wynne Jones, Charmed Life:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(travel) To hitchhike.", "tags": [], "examples": ["So I started thumbin' back east, toward my hometown."], "quotes": [{"text": "Bobby thumbed a diesel down, just before it rained.", "reference": "1969, Kris Kristofferson, Fred Foster, Me and Bobby McGee:"}, {"text": "Thumbed a diesel down, outside a cafe.", "reference": "1980, Kye Fleming, Dennis Morgan, Smoky Mountain Rain:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To soil or wear with the thumb or the fingers; to soil, or wear out, by frequent handling.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "He gravely informed the enemy that all his cards had been thumbed to pieces, and begged them to let him have a few more packs.", "reference": "1849–1861, Thomas Babington Macaulay, chapter XIII, in The History of England from the Accession of James the Second, volume (please specify |volume=I to V), London: Longman, Brown, Green, and Longmans, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To manipulate (an object) with the thumb; especially, to pull back the hammer or open the cylinder of a revolver.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Fargo palmed out his own revolver, thumbing back the hammer as the barrel came up.", "reference": "2009, Jon Sharp, The Trailsman #337: Silver Showdown:"}, {"text": "Rainford reached down and found the revolver. Thumbing the cylinder open, he inspected the load.", "reference": "2015, Tony Monchinski, Bad Men (I Kill Monsters Book 3):"}, {"text": "Andy opened the revolver, thumbed in a cartridge.", "reference": "2015, Don Fitzsimmons, If You Need a Laugh:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To fire (a single action revolver) quickly by pulling the hammer while keeping the trigger depressed.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "To thumb a single-action revolver, hold down the trigger and use the thumb on the